<h1>Email Templates</h1>

<p>
    Email templates help you send consistent, professional emails quickly. Instead of typing the same message over and over, you create a template once and reuse it whenever you need to send that type of email.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Templates page showing the template list on the left and the template editor on the right. Highlight the template editor showing subject line, body text, and the Variables button. Use callouts to identify key areas. -->

<h2>What Are Email Templates?</h2>

<p>
    Email templates are pre-written email messages that you can customize with variables. When you use a template, Quickfire fills in the variables with actual data (like the client's name, policy number, etc.) so the email is personalized automatically.
</p>

<p>
    Templates are perfect for:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Renewal reminders</strong> – Standard messages about upcoming policy expirations</li>
    <li><strong>Quote requests</strong> – Professional requests for quotes from carriers</li>
    <li><strong>Follow-up messages</strong> – Consistent follow-up communications</li>
    <li><strong>Status updates</strong> – Informing clients about policy status</li>
    <li><strong>Any repetitive email</strong> – Messages you send frequently with similar content</li>
</ul>

