<h2>How Templates Work with Outlook</h2>

<p>
    When you use a template to send an email, Quickfire opens Microsoft Outlook with the email already filled in. Here's how it works:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>You select a template (from an agent, action button, or template picker)</li>
    <li>Quickfire fills in all the variables with actual data</li>
    <li>Outlook opens with a new email message</li>
    <li>The subject and body are already populated</li>
    <li>The recipient's email address is filled in (if available)</li>
    <li>You can review, make any final edits, and hit Send</li>
</ol>

<p>
    This approach gives you the best of both worlds: the speed of templates with the flexibility to customize each email before sending.
</p>

