<h2>Template Variables Reference</h2>

<p>
    Here's a more complete list of available variables you can use in templates:
</p>

<h3>Client Variables</h3>
<ul>
    <li>{ClientName} – Company name</li>
    <li>{ClientEmail} – Primary email address</li>
    <li>{ClientName64} – URL-encoded company name (for use in links)</li>
    <li>{ClientEmail64} – URL-encoded email (for use in links)</li>
</ul>

<h3>Policy Variables</h3>
<ul>
    <li>{PolicyNumber} – Policy number</li>
    <li>{PolicyType} – Type of policy</li>
    <li>{PolicyType64} – URL-encoded policy type</li>
    <li>{ExpirationDate} – Policy expiration date</li>
    <li>{EffectiveDate} – Policy effective date</li>
</ul>

<h3>Contact Variables</h3>
<ul>
    <li>{ContactFirstName} – Contact's first name</li>
    <li>{ContactEmail} – Contact's email address</li>
</ul>

<h3>Financial Variables</h3>
<ul>
    <li>{PaymentAmount} – Payment amount (formatted)</li>
    <li>{DownPaymentAmount} – Down payment amount (formatted)</li>
</ul>

<h3>Business Details Variables</h3>
<ul>
    <li>{BusinessDescription} – Description of the business</li>
    <li>{EstimatedGrossSales} – Estimated annual sales</li>
    <li>{EstimatedPayroll} – Estimated annual payroll</li>
    <li>{PrimaryAddress} – Business address</li>
    <li>{PrimaryPhone} – Primary phone number</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The Variables button in the template editor shows all available variables for easy insertion.
</p>

