<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Keep templates current</strong> – Update templates when your messaging changes</li>
    <li><strong>Use clear names</strong> – Name templates descriptively so you can find them easily</li>
    <li><strong>Test variables</strong> – Send a test email to yourself to make sure variables fill in correctly</li>
    <li><strong>Set requirements</strong> – Mark what each template needs so Quickfire can prompt for missing info</li>
    <li><strong>Write professionally</strong> – Templates represent your agency, so make them polished</li>
    <li><strong>Keep it flexible</strong> – Leave room for personalization when needed</li>
</ul>

